> Is `I want this alignment` something you can even do in C?

@niacdoial Sort of, yes. C11 defines an `_Alignas` specifier (macro'd to `alignas` in `<stdalign.h>`) that you can put on variable declarations or struct fields:
```c
#include <stdalign.h>

struct foo {
  alignas(16) void* bar;
};

alignas(32) int quz;
```

But as far as I can tell there's no way to say "this `struct` has this alignment" directly; you need to do it via fields.

```rust
#![feature(generic_assert)]
fn main() {
    std::arch::x86_64::_mm_shuffle_ps(
        todo!(),
        todo!(),
        const {
            assert!(X != 2);
        },
    )
}
```

