It works when `F: for<'a> Fn(&'a i32) -> i32`:
```rust
// wrap closure in this
fn funnel<F: Fn(&i32) -> i32>(f: F) -> F { f }
// or pass in this
fn f(n: &i32) -> i32 { *n * 2 }
```
But not those that input one specific lifetime:
```rust
// passing in this also fails
fn g<'a: 'a>(n: &'a i32) -> i32 { *n * 2 }
```
Presumably the `n: &i32` workaround to guide higher ranked closure inference doesn't work because the annotation on `map_elements` takes precedence and has an input type that is not parameterized with a lifetime. (Moving the annotated closure out of the call site also compiles.)

