@Morgane55440 the issue is about subtyping function items based on subtyping of the implementing type in the qualified paths of the function items.  

In contrast your latest example is just about subtyping of higher-ranked types themselves AFAICT; you compared no function item types.

(`F1` and `F2` must have distinct `TypeId`s, else you could transmute between them (in *either* direction) without `unsafe` (via `dyn Any`), which is unsound.  That would be true even if they weren't related by subtyping.)

