@GuillaumeGomez the `-> _` comes from the cleaning path more than from the delegation itself. `clean_fn_decl_with_params` cleans `decl.output` straight off the HIR, and for a `reuse` item that node is `TyKind::InferDelegation`. `clean_ty` lowers that to `Type::Infer`, which prints as `_`. The HIR honestly has no resolved type there yet; it gets filled in later during analysis. Same reason the inputs come out as `self: _`.

The resolved signature does exist though, just on the ty side. `lower_delegation_ty` pulls it out of `tcx.inherit_sig_for_delegation_item(def_id)`, and `tcx.fn_sig(def_id)` is built on top of that, so `tcx.fn_sig(def_id).instantiate_identity().skip_norm_wip()` hands you the real `PolyFnSig` with the inputs and output filled in. We already clean that exact shape with `clean_poly_fn_sig`, and it does the async sugaring and the `asyncness` check itself. It's the same thing `build_function` does for inlined items, so this isn't a new path, just applying it where the HIR can't help.

What I'd suggest: in the HIR fn path, detect a delegation and clean the middle signature for the decl instead of the HIR one. Detection is cheap: `tcx.hir_opt_delegation_sig_id(def_id).is_some()`, or `decl.opt_delegation_sig_id()`. Roughly:

```rust
if cx.tcx.hir_opt_delegation_sig_id(def_id).is_some() {
    let sig = cx.tcx.fn_sig(def_id).instantiate_identity().skip_norm_wip();
    let decl = clean_poly_fn_sig(cx, Some(def_id), sig);
    return Box::new(Function { decl, generics }); // generics stay HIR-cleaned
}
```

That resolves `-> _` to the real return type and clears up `self: _` as a bonus (the middle path renders `&self` correctly). It also makes the ICE guard moot on this path, since `clean_poly_fn_sig` only sugars when the output is `impl Trait` and `asyncness` reports async.

A couple of things I'd keep separate:
- I'd only clean the decl from the ty side and leave the generics HIR-cleaned. Rerouting the whole function through `build_function`-style cleaning would also pull generics from the middle layer, which is a bigger change, and it drags in the `<Self>` rendering. That one shows up for plain sync delegation too, so it feels like its own issue rather than part of this fix.
- Worth checking on the test: `asyncness(delegation_def_id)` needs to report async for the sugaring to fire, otherwise the output renders as `impl Future<...>` instead of the sugared form. Still better than `_`, but worth confirming.

The only real plumbing is that `clean_function` / `clean_fn_decl_with_params` don't get the item `DefId` today, so it has to be threaded in from the callers, which all have it.

