> 1. The  "expected `u32`" is suspicous. Is this from the fallback of integer types?

No, this is because `Duration` only implements `Div<Rhs>` for `Rhs = u32`, not any other type, so the compiler infers that `some_duration / something` means that `something` should be `u32`.

I think somewhere else in the compiler that's producing the suggestion probably assumes that if it sees a type error like "expected integer1, found integer2" ("expected u32, found u128") on a binary operator, that the other side of the operator is an `integer2` (and thus suggests converting whichever operand is the narrower integer type to the wider integer type), which is not a correct assumption. If this is the case, that code should probably check the actual type of the other side of the operator before emitting the suggestion.


