I had a go at minimizing it. Seems like `-Ctarget-feature=+avx512dq,+avx512vl` is the minimal set of features needed. Additionally, it seems like the array's len also has to be at least 16, otherwise it won't get vectorized, and the miscompilation happens only at `a[i]` where `i mod 4 == 2` (not sure why this happens). The `black_box` is also needed to make sure the loop doesn't get unrolled.

```rs
// rustc -O -Ctarget-feature=+avx512dq,+avx512vl bad.rs

fn main() {
    let mut a = [0.0f64; 16];
    a[2] = -1.0;

    let mut out = [0i128; 16];
    for i in 0..std::hint::black_box(a.len()) {
        let bits = a[i].to_bits();
        let mag = a[i].abs().to_bits() as i128;
        out[i] = if bits == 0 {
            0
        } else if (bits as i64) < 0 {
            -mag
        } else {
            mag
        };
    }

    assert!(out[2] < 0, "got {}", out[2]);
}
```
